#: contactMatrix.md:82
msgid "Optimisation details"
msgstr "最適化の詳細"

#: contactMatrix.md:84
msgid ""
"The contact matrix is sparse. Each atom is only be connected to a small "
"number of neighbours and the vast majority of the elements of the contact "
"matrix are thus zero. To reduce the amount of memory that PLUMED requires I "
"have thus implemented sparse matrix storage. If you do calculate and store a"
" contact matrix only the elements of the matrix that are non-zero are "
"stored."
msgstr "Contact は疎で、各原子は少数の Neighbor だけに接続します。Memory を減らすため非0要素だけを保存します。"

#: contactMatrix.md:88
msgid ""
"We can also use the sparsity of the contact matrix to make the time required"
" to compute a contact matrix scale linearly rather than quadratically with "
"the number of atoms. Element $i,j$ of the contact matrix is only non-zero if"
" two atoms are within a cutoff, $r_c$. We can determine that many pairs of "
"atoms are further appart than $r_c$ without computing the distance between "
"these atoms by using divide and conquer strategies such as linked lists and "
"neighbour lists. These optimisation tricks are implemented in the base class"
" AgencyMatrixBase. This class therefore ensures that only the subset of "
"elements of the contact matrix that are definitely non-zero are computed. "
"Furthermore, because coordination numbers are computed within the chain of "
"actions only the non-zero elements of the matrix are propegated onwards "
"through the chain when we multiply by the vector of ones. In the flowchart "
"diagrams that I have shown previously the blue subgraphs illustrate how data"
" is passed through actions as the elements of the matrix row are evaluated."
msgstr ""
"疎性で時間も原子数の二乗から線形にできます。要素 $i,j$ が非0なのは距離 $r_c$ 内だけなので、Linked List・Neighbor "
"List の Divide-and-conquer で $r_c$ 外の多くを距離計算なしで除外します。AgencyMatrixBase "
"がこの最適化を担い、非0だけを計算します。全1 Vector の積も非0だけを後続に渡します。Flow Chart の青い Subgraph "
"は行の要素評価時の伝達を示します。"

